Operator      Consumed    Produced            Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
sam_rbt       x y         -                   Set the rbt region to reference positions x..y (for the rbt_ operators) [sam]
rbt_refx      -           p                   rbt: first reference position (region clipped to the matched part) [sam]
rbt_refy      -           p                   rbt: last reference position [sam]
rbt_dx        -           n                   rbt: positions cut off at the start (rbt_refx - x) [sam]
rbt_dy        -           n                   rbt: positions cut off at the end (y - rbt_refy) [sam]
rbt_qryx      -           p                   rbt: first query position [sam]
rbt_qryy      -           p                   rbt: last query position [sam]
rbt_qrylen    -           n                   rbt: query length [sam]
rbt_qry       -           seq                 rbt: query sequence [sam]
rbt_nmatch    -           n                   rbt: aligned bases (| x) [sam]
rbt_nmatchx   -           n                   rbt: mismatched aligned bases (x) [sam]
rbt_ndel      -           n                   rbt: deleted bases (-) [sam]
rbt_nins      -           n                   rbt: inserted bases (~) [sam]
rbt_nedit     -           n                   rbt: edits (- ~ x) [sam]
rbt_alnref    -           aln                 rbt: the region's columns of aln_ref [sam]
rbt_alnaln    -           aln                 rbt: the region's columns of aln_aln [sam]
rbt_alnqry    -           aln                 rbt: the region's columns of aln_qry [sam]
rbt_alnrlr    -           aln                 rbt: the region's columns of aln_rlr [sam]
rbt_alnqlt    -           aln                 rbt: the region's columns of aln_qlt [sam]
rbt_alnall    -           aln                 rbt: ruler, reference, match, query, quality lines of the region [sam]

Use -l TERM.. for a category or the operators whose name contains TERM.
